  "title": "Class-4 pair failures are #P-hard if gadget counts are local up to a Massey-type relabeling",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "If zero-jump gadget counts are local up to a relabeling of degree-3 data, the indeterminacy of a Massey-type obstruction, then linear flows on single edges keep the Fourier dual non-negative even with independent potentials at the two ends of an edge, so counting is #P-hard. Six class-4 census algebras satisfy the single-edge conditions, so they are #P-hard if that locality holds.",
